cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Temari: atomic scattering and excitation factors from first principles"
message: "If you use this software or the tables it generates, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Seto
    given-names: Yusuke
    email: seto77@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/seto77/Temari"
url: "https://seto77.github.io/Temari/"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/seto77/Temari/blob/main/licenses/README.md"
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-08-10"
keywords:
  - electron microscopy
  - EELS
  - STEM-EDX
  - inner-shell ionization
  - generalized oscillator strength
  - atomic form factor
  - Dirac-Hartree-Fock-Slater
  - Julia
abstract: >-
  Temari solves an isolated atom from scratch — self-consistent field, bound
  orbitals and distorted continuum waves — and derives the scattering and
  excitation factors used by electron microscopy, spectroscopy and transport
  simulation: the inner-shell ionization form factor F(s, E0) for STEM-EDX, the
  EELS differential cross section, the generalized oscillator strength, X-ray
  and electron atomic scattering factors, and Mott elastic cross sections. It
  depends on the Julia standard library only and contains no fitted parameter
  tables, with one declared exception (the public-domain Bote–Salvat ionization
  cross-section coefficients; see CONTRIBUTING.md). Generated datasets carry
  their own version, independent of this software version, are distributed
  separately under CC-BY-4.0 while the software itself is MIT, and each is
  pinned to a specific Julia release in its manifest. The prescription was chosen and
  verified by the author; the bulk of the implementation was written by an AI
  assistant (Anthropic Claude) under that direction.
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: >-
      Inner-shell ionization form factors F(s, E0) for STEM-EDX: 525 channels
      (K, L1-L3, M1-M5) computed with Temari
    authors:
      - family-names: Seto
        given-names: Yusuke
    version: "5.0.0"
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21872050"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    notes: >-
      Dataset v5.0.0, released separately from this software and under different
      terms (CC-BY-4.0; the software is MIT). Cite this version DOI for
      reproducibility -- it guarantees the files have not changed. The
      version-independent DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21872049 resolves to the latest
      version instead. A byte-identical mirror is attached to the GitHub release
      dataset-v5.0.0; the archive is built deterministically so the two copies
      can be compared rather than merely trusted.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Cross sections for ionization of inner shells of atoms by electron impact
    authors:
      - family-names: Bote
        given-names: David
      - family-names: Salvat
        given-names: Francesc
      - family-names: Jablonski
        given-names: Aleksander
