      Source of the bundled absolute ionization cross-section parameterization
      (src/bote_salvat.json). See also the Erratum, At. Data Nucl. Data Tables
      97, 186 (2011).
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Calculations of inner-shell ionization by electron impact with the
      distorted-wave and plane-wave Born approximations
    authors:
      - family-names: Bote
        given-names: David
      - family-names: Salvat
        given-names: Francesc
    journal: "Physical Review A"
    volume: 77
    start: 042701
    year: 2008
    doi: "10.1103/PhysRevA.77.042701"
    notes: >-
      The relativistic distorted-wave calculations that the bundled
      parameterization was fitted to.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Relativistic EELS scattering cross-sections for microanalysis based on
      Dirac solutions
    authors:
      - family-names: Zhang
        given-names: Zezhong
      - family-names: Lobato
        given-names: Ivan
      - family-names: Brown
        given-names: Hamish
      - family-names: Lamoen
        given-names: Dirk
      - family-names: Jannis
        given-names: Daen
      - family-names: Verbeeck
        given-names: Johan
      - family-names: Van Aert
        given-names: Sandra
      - family-names: Nellist
        given-names: Peter D.
    year: 2024
    doi: "10.48550/arXiv.2405.10151"
    notes: >-
      No code, parameters or tabulated values from this work are bundled here.
      It is cited because (a) the relativistic-electrodynamics interaction
      kernel, the small-component radial matrix element and the kappa-resolved
      angular factor are implemented from the equations as presented in this
      paper (equations 38-41; the underlying physics is standard relativistic
      scattering theory, and equation 38 as printed is missing a q^2 in the
      transverse denominator, corrected here and cross-checked against the
      paper's own equation 42), and (b) the authors' open Dirac GOS database
      (Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.7729585, CC-BY) is used as an external comparison
      target during verification. The database itself is not redistributed.
